-- title:
--   Ends, residue discs and valuative cover at a supersingular place, q=2
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q=2$, $M'$ is a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$, and $\ell_g$ is a prime with $\ell_g\equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$. Further, $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$ in the sense of `LiesOverPrime` (that is, $q$ is a nonunit of $A$), with residue field $\kappa=$ `ResidueField A`; $W$ is a finite set of places of the $\kappa$-function field `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` (the $\kappa$-subfield of Laurent series generated by the two $j$-expansions `jqModC` and `jqNModC`) whose members are, by `hW`, exactly the supersingular places, i.e. those $w$ that are rational, are affine geometric places, and have $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of `jGeomGen` in the supersingular $j$-set `ssJSet q κ`; `hle` records the inclusion of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` (the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base change of the full modular function field of level $M'$) in `fieldBar q M'`, the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-Laurent-series function field at level $q^2M'$ cut out by the subgroup `levelH q M'` (the kernel of reduction of units modulo $q$). The reduction datum is a `ConstantReduction` $R_0$ of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` — a valuation subring of integers, a surjective residue map with kernel the maximal ideal, a map on places preserving degrees, compatibility with constants and divisors — together with the hypothesis `hR₀` that every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in $R_0$'s integers and has $R_0$-residue equal to the coefficientwise residue of $y$. Finally $s\in W$ is a chosen supersingular place.
--
--   The small-constant data consist of an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and an element $\pi_0\in k_0$ lying in $A$, subject to: the contraction $A\cap k_0$ is a discrete valuation ring, its maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$, it is Henselian, its residue field is algebraically closed, and (`hκ`) every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0\cap A$.
--
--   The auxiliary data consist of a prime $\ell$ with $3\le\ell$, $\ell\neq q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$; an element $\zeta_0\in k_0$ which is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; and an element $\varpi_t\in k_0$ lying in $A$ with $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\cdot u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$. A layer family is given by a type $\iota$, intermediate fields $K_n$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$, each finite over $k_0$, valuation subrings $A_n\subseteq K_n$ tracing $A$, an index $n_0$ with $K_{n_0}\le K_n$ for all $n$, and the cofinality hypothesis `hKcof` that every finite subset of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is contained in some $K_n$. Moreover $\pi_t\in\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $A$ and satisfies $\pi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q$, and `htame` asserts that every element $\tau$ of the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb Q$ with `A.tameCharacter πt τ` $=1$ fixes $K_{n_0}$ pointwise. The base presentation consists of $K_b=\bot$ as an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$, a valuation subring $A_b\subseteq K_b$ tracing $A$, and a nonzero $\varpi_b$ generating the maximal ideal of $A_b$.
--
--   With `fieldBar q M'` regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $k_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$, the assertion is made for every intermediate field $F_0$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $k_0$ satisfying four conditions: $f\in F_0$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $f$ lies in $k_0$; the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is everything; $F_0$ is stable under the level automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` for every $\zeta$ in `Idx q` (the primitive $q$-th roots of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$) and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')\subseteq\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$; and a linear-disjointness clause: for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, every finite family $c_i\in\overline{\mathbb Q}$ linearly independent over $K'$ and every family $a_i$ in the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i=0$ forces all $a_i=0$.
--
--   Further data are: a valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$; a subring $B$ of `fieldBar q M'` with an $A_b$-algebra structure; the hypotheses `hjR` that the class of $j$ (the image under `coeffEmb` of the Laurent series `jq`) lies in $R_0$'s integers and `hjs` that its $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$; `hJK` that `jqNModC` $\overline{\mathbb Q}\,q$ lies in `fieldBar q M'`; an element $a_0\in k_0$ lying in $A$ with `hpin`: the residue of $a_0$ in $\kappa$ raised to the $q$-th power equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $j$; and a finite set `nodes` of subrings of $F_0$.
--
--   For these the following hypothesis block (a single conjunction, whose groups are named here) is assumed. *Centre clauses*: $W_0$ traces $A$ on the constants $k_0$; $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring; $\pi_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates its maximal ideal. *Specialisation at $s$*: for every Laurent series $g$ in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose base-changed class lies in $R_0$'s integers, which is regular wherever $j$ is (at every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, $0\le P.\mathrm{ord}\,j$ implies $0\le P.\mathrm{ord}\,g$) and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $g$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$, and for every $c\in k_0\cap A$ whose residue in $\kappa$ equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that $R_0$-residue, the difference of the image of $g$ and $c$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_0$. *Level invariance of $W_0$*: for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and $f\in F_0$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` $f\in F_0$, membership of $f$ in $W_0$ is equivalent to membership of its image. *Chart clauses for $B$*: the $A_b$-algebra structure is the one induced by $K_b\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$; $B$ is contained in the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K_b$, and every element of that join is a ratio $g/h$ with $g,h\in B$, $h\neq0$; $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_b$; the quotient of $B$ by $\varpi_b$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; every element of $B$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$; $\varpi_b$ is prime in $B$; $W_0$ consists exactly of the ratios $g/h$ with $g,h\in B$ and $\varpi_b\nmid h$; $j$ lies in $B$; $B$ is stable under the level automorphisms for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; there is an element $b$ of $B\cap F_0$ lying outside every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ that traces $A$ on $k_0$, has $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal, contains $j$, and is such that no monic polynomial over $k_0$ with $A$-integral coefficients takes a value at $j$ lying in the maximal ideal of $V$; and, for every $s'\in W$ distinct from $s$, there is an element $b$ of $B\cap F_0$ lying outside every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ tracing $A$ on $k_0$ and satisfying the specialisation clause above with $s'$ and $V$ in place of $s$ and $W_0$. *Drinfeld clause*: for every $\mathrm{GF}(q^2)$-algebra structure on $\kappa$, every proof that [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) is a domain and every $\zeta$ in `Idx q`, there are a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathrm{GF}(q^2)$ and a ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B$ to [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) with: $\#C_s=$ `placeWidthChar q M' s` (the $q$-adapted $j$-width at $s$ divided by the ramification of $j$ at $s$); kernel of $\rho$ the ideal generated by $\varpi_b$; $\rho$ compatible with $A_b\to\kappa$ and the structure map; every element of the target a ratio $\rho(g)/\rho(h)$; the image of $\rho$ consisting exactly of those elements coming from the coordinate ring inside the Drinfeld function field; and equivariance: for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,1)$ in `hSubgroup q` and $f\in B$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` $f\in B$, $\rho$ of the latter equals `hFunctionFieldAction` at that element applied to $\rho(f)$. *Node clauses*: `nodes` has exactly $q+1$ members; there is a subring $B_c$ of $F_0$, generated by the $A$-integral constants of $k_0$ together with a finite set, contained in every node $O$ and such that each $O$ is the localisation of $B_c$ at its units ($f\in O$ iff $f\cdot h=g$ with $g,h\in B_c$ and $h$ a unit of $O$); the level automorphisms permute `nodes`, and for every $\zeta$ any two nodes are carried one to the other by some $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; distinct nodes are separated by an element that is a nonunit in one and a unit in the other; every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ tracing $A$ on $k_0$ and satisfying the specialisation clause at $s$ either contains all of $B$ or contains a node $O$ all of whose nonunits lie in the maximal ideal of $V$; and each node $O$ satisfies: $O\subseteq W_0$; $O$ is local and Noetherian; $O$ traces $A$ on $k_0$; every element of $O$ is congruent to an $A$-integral constant (its difference with some such constant is a nonunit of $O$); and there are an integer $E_0\ge1$ with $\pi_0^{E_0}=\varpi_t^{\,\mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s}\cdot v$ for a unit $v$ of $k_0\cap A$, elements $c_x,c_y\in O$, a unit $u$ of $O$, an isomorphism of the adic completion of $O$ at its maximal ideal with the crossing model `UVCrossingModel` over the adic completion of $A\cap k_0$ with parameter $\pi_0^{E_0}$ (that is, a two-variable power series ring modulo $XY-\pi_0^{E_0}$), and units $\gamma_U,\gamma_V$ of that model, such that $c_xc_y=\pi_0^{E_0}u$, constants go to constants, $c_x$ and $c_y$ correspond to $\gamma_U\cdot U$ and $\gamma_V\cdot V$, $c_y$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_0$ while $c_x$ does not, and in addition: the element `jqNModC` $\overline{\mathbb Q}\,q$ minus $a_0$ lies in $F_0$ and in $O$ and corresponds to a unit times $V^e$ for some $e\ge1$; there is a valuation subring $W_x$ of $F_0$ containing $O$, tracing $A$, discrete with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, carrying an element $t$ such that a polynomial over $k_0$ with $A$-integral coefficients whose value at $t$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ has all coefficients there, with $c_x$ in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ and $c_y$ not, and such that every $g$ as in the specialisation clause (in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'`, $R_0$-integral, regular where $j$ is) has image in $F_0$ and in $W_x$, lying in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ exactly when its $R_0$-residue vanishes, and, when that residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, lying in $O$ and differing from each matching $A$-integral constant by a nonunit of $O$; and there is a subring $B_x$ of $F_0$ whose elements lie in $B$ and in $O$ and are regular wherever $j$ is at places of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, of which $O$ is the localisation at its units, with fraction field $F_0$, generated by the $A$-integral constants together with a finite set, and containing an element $b$ lying outside every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ which traces $A$, has $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal, contains $j$ with no monic $A$-integral polynomial value at $j$ in the maximal ideal, and fails to contain some element of $O$.
--
--   Under these hypotheses the conclusion is: for every field $F_{ss}$ which is an algebra over $\kappa$ and every `RegularProlongation` $R$ of $A$ from `fieldBar q M'` to $F_{ss}$ (a valuation subring of integers tracing $A$, a surjective residue map onto $F_{ss}$ with kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with constants, and such that every nonzero element becomes integral with nonzero residue after scaling by a constant) such that for $f\in F_0$ membership in $R$'s integers is equivalent to membership in $W_0$, there exists a finite set $N_e$ of places of $F_{ss}$ over $\kappa$ with the following four properties.
--
--   First, $N_e$ has exactly $q+1$ elements. Second, a place $Q$ of $F_{ss}$ lies outside $N_e$ if and only if for every $b\in B$ whose image lies in $R$'s integers the $R$-residue of $b$ lies in the valuation subring of $Q$. Third, every $Q\notin N_e$ carries a residue disc: there are a set $D$ of places of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and an element $z$ with `R.IsResidueDisc Q D z`, i.e. $z$ is a disc coordinate (each $P\in D$ is rational, contains $z$ with $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,z$ less than $1$; $z$ is $R$-integral with $Q.\mathrm{ord}$ of its residue equal to $1$; each constant of valuation less than $1$ is attained as $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,z$ for exactly one $P\in D$; $z$ minus its value has order $1$ at each $P\in D$; and a unit principle holds for functions with no zeros or poles on $D$), the pointwise compatibility of $R$-residues with values at rational places of $D$ holds, and the degree formula holds (the sum of the orders along $D$ of an $R$-integral function with nonzero residue equals the order of that residue at $Q$); moreover every $P\in D$ satisfies $0\le P.\mathrm{ord}\,j$ and contains all of $B$ in its valuation subring. Fourth, for every rational place $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ which is centred at $s$ — meaning that for every $R_0$-integral $f$ regular wherever $j$ is and with $R_0$-residue in the valuation subring of $s$, and every $a\in A$ whose residue equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that residue, the value $P.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the image of $f$ differs from $a$ by an element of the maximal ideal of $A$ — either some node $O\in$ `nodes` is contained in the valuation subring of $P$ and each nonunit of $O$ has its $P$-value in the maximal ideal of $A$, or there is a place $Q\notin N_e$ with a residue disc $(D,z)$ for $R$ at $Q$ containing $P$.
--
--   This is the step, for the excluded prime $q=2$ at a rigid auxiliary level, that identifies the $q+1$ ends of the base affine chart of the descended regular model of the modular curve along the supersingular tube at $s$, equips each non-end place of the reduced field with a residue disc on which the chart is regular and $j$ has no pole, and shows that every rational place centred at $s$ is either captured by one of the $q+1$ node rings or lies in one of these discs. It feeds the construction of node presentations and node charts with the Hasse parameter, namely [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.klevel_nodePresentations_nodeCharts_hasseJ_of_affineChart_poles_hasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_of_eq_two_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.klevel_nodePresentations_nodeCharts_hasseJ_of_affineChart_poles_hasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_of_eq_two_of_dvd).
